WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:07.323
A normalized operational database and an analytical
model solve different problems OLTP

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:13.326
systems focus on safe day-to-day transactions They
reduce duplicated facts protect

00:00:13.352 --> 00:00:19.133
updates and use keys and constraints to preserve
integrity Analytical

00:00:19.159 --> 00:00:24.833
models focus on understandable efficient reporting
Fact tables store measurable

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:30.649
events while dimensions provide descriptive context
That means a star

00:00:30.676 --> 00:00:35.228
schema may intentionally repeat some descriptive
values in ways an operational schema

00:00:35.241 --> 00:00:41.291
would avoid The important point is that dimensional
modeling complements the normalized

00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:47.267
source It does not excuse poor operational design A

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.004
trustworthy analytical model is easier to build when
the source system has

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:56.412
clear grain reliable identifiers controlled
relationships and well-enforced business rules
